Falsifies `system_tests::user::every_core_tick_budget_tests::a_wait_on_every_core_outlasts_a_core_that_takes_no_ticks`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is `EveryCoreTickBudget::is_expired` deciding on the counter alone, the seeded fuzz
drivers' two-second wall-clock deadline: the budget runs out once two seconds of the counter have
passed, whether or not every core took its ticks. Another core spends three seconds of the counter
with its interrupts masked, a stand-in for a vCPU the host is not running, so the wait gives up a
second before the work it waits on finishes.

Expected to fail: `panic!("the wait gave up while a core took no ticks: {budget}")`, with about
2000 ms of the counter and one core showing far fewer ticks than the other. Confirmed red on
2026-10-31 (UTC) on x86_64 at two cores with `cargo xtask test --arch x86_64 --test
a_wait_on_every_core_outlasts`: "2000 ms of the counter; ticks taken of 200 on each core: core 0
198 core 1 0". Replayed red again after the counts became `u32`: "core 0 199 core 1 0".

